{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T11:42:22.077Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Both the task verify (`node --import tsx --test tests/baseline-verify.test.ts` — 9/9 pass) and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify` — exit 0, 2185 CLI tests + 88 UI tests, 0 fails, lint clean) pass.\n\nSummary of what landed:\n- **`src/watcher/baseline.ts`** (new): `settleBaseline` no-ops when the gate is unset or any task stream already holds `started`; selects/keys via `selectVcs`/`readBaselineKey`; reuses the latest green `baseline_ran` across active/archived `change.jsonl` streams when command+commit+digest match; otherwise runs the command in the project root with a null change folder, records `baseline_ran`, and returns a `baseline_red` failure with the halt line.\n- **`src/watcher/runner.ts`**: two lines plus the import, right after `verifyCtx` and before `runPreSpawnVerify` (196 lines, still under the 200-line budget).\n- **`src/harness/types.ts`** and **`src/watcher/failure-reason.ts`**: new `baseline_ran` event + `BaselineRanEventData`, and `baseline_red`.\n- **`tests/baseline-verify.test.ts`** (new): all delta scenarios, the proposal's red-before-the-change and changed-tracked/untracked reuse cases, and that the default `autoRetries` leaves `baseline_red` dead.\n- **`README.md`** and **`osq.config.ts`** updated per the proposal.\n\nOne deviation is recorded in the result file: `formatTaskOutcomeLine` (out of scope) places the extra before `elapsed`, so the halt line appears in the outcome line but not at its very end; the dead marker's first body line is exactly the phrase."}}
